The derived rule is present at priority 20, but the backend still selects the built-in `#while` step; the blocker is its large exact module-map match, not the induction theorem itself. The loop reads only the local `n` and `divisor`, so I’m strengthening and simplifying the proved invariant to be parametric in the entire surrounding scope map. The derived rule can then match just the active local frame.
