codex
I found the composition mismatch: the Python semantics keeps the remaining statements as a `Stmts` list in the continuation. The proof had used individual `Stmt` items separated by `~>`, which looks nearly identical when pretty-printed but is a different K term. I’m correcting the loop invariant and entry-prefix destination to use the exact `Stmts` continuation shape produced by the supplied sequencing rule.
apply patch
